<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:58:18Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>'Life in Gaza simply miserable': Amid flooding, lack of aid, conditions 'worsen' for Palestinians</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a57f3b727e3f7514a63336fd3fcccbc86b7fff06edfb4d2be0d25d4ec00402f</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:57:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T17:26:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/life-in-gaza-simply-miserable-amid-flooding-lack-of-aid-conditions-worsen-for-palestinians--d44b8a8693f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/life-in-gaza-simply-miserable-amid-flooding-lack-of-aid-conditions-worsen-for-palestinians" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Shaina Low, Communication Adviser for the Norwegian Refugee Council (NRC). Thirteen months into what she describes as a "so-called ceasefire," the humanitarian crisis in Gaza continues to deepen, exposing the profound gap between diplomatic commitments and the lived realities of Palestinian civilians. In an interview with France 24, Shayna Low, communications adviser in Palestine for the Norwegian Refugee Council (NRC), describes a population confronting winter flooding, repeated displacement, deteriorating shelter conditions and persistent restrictions on humanitarian assistance. "Life in Gaza is simply miserable." Low urges Israel to "open all the crossings, lift the restrictions, let aid in."</summary></entry><entry><title>Social unrest ahead of French elections:  Protesters 'don't believe politics can achieve anything'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd442b2dee855baab9e5d12e913a14a73ec4555fa48229b3f40269b0c3b7c3d7</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:57:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:52:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/social-unrest-ahead-of-french-elections-protesters-don-t-believe-politics-can-achieve-anything--cc8dffe6ee66.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/social-unrest-ahead-of-french-elections-protesters-don-t-believe-politics-can-achieve-anything" /><summary type="html">Annette Young is pleased to welcome Renaud Foucart, Senior Lecturer at the Department of Economics ECARES at Lancaster University. France's 1.6% minimum-wage increase, in response to the countrywide protests, may offer a temporary reprieve from social unrest, but it does little to resolve the deeper political and institutional crisis confronting the country. According to Foucart, the central problem extends beyond declining purchasing power, fiscal constraints and the limitations of a minority government. It concerns a growing loss of faith in politics itself. “They are in the street because they don't believe politics can achieve anything,” Foucart argues, suggesting that the persistence of mass demonstrations ahead of the presidential election reflects profound disillusionment with the political system's capacity to deliver meaningful change.</summary></entry><entry><title>French PM brings forward hike in minimum wage to calm protesters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c0b7ffa634de391da7e1db5248a6a91e912be0cbf94ab1620653f76334eebb3b</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:57:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:47:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-french-pm-brings-forward-hike-in-minimum-wage-to-calm-protesters--1f3e775b1585.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-french-pm-brings-forward-hike-in-minimum-wage-to-calm-protesters" /><summary type="html">French Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu said ​on Monday, November 9, he was bringing forward a planned hike in the minimum wage to December from January, as he sought to defuse a cost-of-living crisis that has sparked some of France's worst civil unrest in years. Unions swiftly dismissed the offer as "crumbs".</summary></entry><entry><title>Nvidia shares tumble after spy probe announced</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8400e38172357aced6a65f9e69de922b6e9daa4284d1825be2c200e9e3c2fb41</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:57:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:47:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-nvidia-shares-tumble-after-spy-probe-announced--b82780c21853.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-nvidia-shares-tumble-after-spy-probe-announced" /><summary type="html">Shares of artificial intelligence leader Nvidia tumbled early Monday after the chip company said it launched an investigation of CEO Jensen Huang following reports he was targeted by Chinese intelligence. Nvidia shares were down more than eight percent in opening trading after its board announced that a committee of independent directors assisted by outside counsel would undertake the probe.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Iran's Revolutionary Guards behind cyberattacks on supermarket fridges, says French FM</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:98bb8d11d09d0dfa55d708076e34168143d37e70aa3d159733213be347f5d74e</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:57:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:44:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-iran-revolutionary-guards-behind-cyberattacks-on-supermarket-fridges-says-french-fm-barrot--977c1baab94e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-iran-revolutionary-guards-behind-cyberattacks-on-supermarket-fridges-says-french-fm-barrot" /></entry><entry><title>Russell Brand sentenced to 10-and-a-half years in jail for rape, sexual assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95d0e71052145bc7876adfa808f4c90d970cbdaec020c5026a1a21ff08d3cf99</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:57:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:43:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-russell-brand-sentenced-to-10-and-a-half-years-in-jail-for-rape-sexual-assault--dbd738f4fd45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-russell-brand-sentenced-to-10-and-a-half-years-in-jail-for-rape-sexual-assault" /><summary type="html">British comedian Russell Brand, once one of the country's most high-profile broadcasters and a Hollywood star, was jailed for 10-and-a-half years on Monday after he was convicted of raping one woman and sexually assaulting three others around two decades ago.  The judge said ‌Brand was a sexual predator who believed "fame meant you could act how you liked, when you liked, unhindered by the rules ⁠by which decent people live".</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran's Revolutionary Guards behind cyberattacks on supermarket fridges, says French FM</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b239299d2720ee99350051964615030e73eda4335416e0c7af4cce2d131b244e</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:57:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:42:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-iran-revolutionary-guards-behind-cyberattacks-on-supermarket-fridges-says-french-fm-barrot--977c1baab94e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-iran-revolutionary-guards-behind-cyberattacks-on-supermarket-fridges-says-french-fm-barrot" /><summary type="html">French Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot on Monday accused Iran's Revolutionary Guards of being behind a recent cyberattack on French supermarket fridges, saying there would be consequences for the country. The Paris prosecutor's office said it had opened an investigation into an Iranian cyber unit affiliated with the Guards over the cyberattacks.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia in turmoil as China denies spying claims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:641fa533b6c94573c63f789eebf7f2215f44377670e209a9ff2a66eb64bcd9da</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:57:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:42:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-nvidia-in-turmoil-as-china-denies-spying-claims--3bd125f665d4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-nvidia-in-turmoil-as-china-denies-spying-claims" /><summary type="html">Nvidia shares tumbled this Monday after the AI chipmaking giant said it would investigate its CEO's affair with a suspected Chinese spy. There are concerns Jensen Huang was targeted by a foreign intelligence effort following a media report that he had a close relationship with a Chinese businesswoman who allegedly passed information to Beijing. China, meanwhile, has slammed the spying allegations as a "smear campaign".</summary></entry><entry><title>'Sexual predator' Russell Brand jailed for 10 years for rape, assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54c15bb7921846f99cc8c87e5c4f8a89d33728eaa82fe89b88130bce4735ad0d</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:57:33Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:16:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-sexual-predator-russell-brand-jailed-for-10-years-for-rape-assault--8261ff0a2a6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-sexual-predator-russell-brand-jailed-for-10-years-for-rape-assault" /><summary type="html">British comedian and TV star Russell Brand was Monday jailed for more than 10 years for a string of sex offences including rape as the judge told him he had been a "sexual predator" whose fame had protected him.</summary></entry><entry><title>COP31 climate summit: Can we electrify the world?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e40a908e332cf38f02b9671e8b9673cc0b6b9b95d10bbaec7e343019a5c45b85</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:57:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:00:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261109-cop31-climate-summit-can-we-electrify-the-world--f589e28f7096.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261109-cop31-climate-summit-can-we-electrify-the-world" /><summary type="html">The UN's annual climate change summit, known as COP31, opens this Monday in Turkey amid deep concern following deadly heatwaves in Europe and deadly floods in Nepal. A "super El Niño" in the Pacific is also expected to drive more extreme weather events. In response, COP31 host Turkey is set to launch a global initiative aiming to electrify a third of the world economy. FRANCE 24's Environment Editor Valerie Dekimpe tells us more.</summary><category term="Down to Earth" /></entry><entry><title>'Such an extraordinary story': What we know so far about Nvidia spying claims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54940aeefbcb2b387486b912b287a3843d95a1bceb7807cd699a91aff2ee6439</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:57:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T15:54:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-such-an-extraordinary-story-what-we-know-so-far-about-nvidia-spying-claims--45fab7bcde9f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-such-an-extraordinary-story-what-we-know-so-far-about-nvidia-spying-claims" /><summary type="html">Shares of artificial intelligence leader Nvidia tumbled early Monday after the chip company said it launched an investigation of CEO Jensen Huang following reports he was targeted by Chinese intelligence. The internal probe comes after a media report that Huang had a close relationship with a Chinese businesswoman who allegedly passed information to Beijing. France 24's Philip Turle takes a look at what we know so far about the allegations.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain's right holds poll lead over Sanchez's Socialists ahead of November 29 snap election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:433cc8d3f59441eb4a12424d8f7c4cc7bbb43e7d3c3e13e441c69b0706968f8a</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:57:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T15:46:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-spain-right-leads-sanchez-socialists-in-polls-for-november-29-snap-election--1d062be0599a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-spain-right-leads-sanchez-socialists-in-polls-for-november-29-snap-election" /><summary type="html">Spain's ruling Socialists have narrowed the gap but continue to trail the conservative People's Party, who would need to team up with the far-right Vox party to secure a majority of seats in parliament, pollsters say with three weeks to go before the country's general election.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian network used social media to blame French riots on immigration, EU report says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:939bdf071ff2f0859a538b795bb79cbcab0d260deacab1f9ef5d94b2faf8d9d8</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:57:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T15:38:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261109-russian-network-used-social-media-to-blame-french-riots-on-immigration-eu-report-says--8b657448aae3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261109-russian-network-used-social-media-to-blame-french-riots-on-immigration-eu-report-says" /><summary type="html">An internal EU assessment has uncovered a Russian network that aimed to exploit ​last month's riots in France by using social media to blame the unrest on uncontrolled immigration. The assessment, seen by Reuters, offers an insight into how external actors have been exploiting France's domestic turmoil for their ⁠own political ends.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Melanie C: From Sporty Spice to dance DJ with 'Sweat'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95c1bca8df92f40f11534e80e8706f58f0bc0f8dc3d73ba0b12765fa58ed18e6</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:57:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T15:37:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261109-melanie-c-from-sporty-spice-to-dance-dj-with-sweat--134cdf19830f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261109-melanie-c-from-sporty-spice-to-dance-dj-with-sweat" /><summary type="html">Melanie Chisholm rose to fame in the 1990s with one of the world's biggest girl bands: the Spice Girls. "Melanie C", "Mel C" and "Sporty Spice" were her nicknames. She went on to have a successful solo career with several hits in the 2000s, including "Never Be The Same Again" with the late Lisa Left Eye from TLC. In recent years, she's taken up DJing electronic dance music and recently released her ninth studio album "Sweat". Marjorie Hache caught up with the fitter-than-ever ex-Spice Girl.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Shock and grief in Poland after weekend mass shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9cd5fe520861a78bd8e1b27e9181d051de9442ef5954cf4947b5a6cf38f457c5</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:57:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T15:31:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-shock-and-grief-in-poland-after-weekend-mass-shooting--e6f1c827a5aa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-shock-and-grief-in-poland-after-weekend-mass-shooting" /><summary type="html">Poland was in shock after a weekend mass shooting in which a gunman opened fire, killing six people and wounding 15 in the city of Krakow before police shot and wounded him. The shooter died in the hospital on Monday morning, police said.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nvidia CEO probed over alleged China spy: Who exactly is Jensen Huang?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a191eb07d2b22a5dfd414e36d3dbc469ee9dd6cad6ccdc457aceacc815ee6b8b</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:57:54Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T15:26:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-nvidia-ceo-probed-over-alleged-china-spy-who-exactly-is-jensen-huang--d5c28f6e3627.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-nvidia-ceo-probed-over-alleged-china-spy-who-exactly-is-jensen-huang" /><summary type="html">AI chip behemoth Nvidia was plunged into turmoil Monday, November 9, after its high-profile CEO Jensen Huang acknowledged having an affair, with reports saying US officials believe the woman was spying for China. But who exactly is Jensen Huang, and why does this case matter so much?</summary></entry><entry><title>Chef Alan Geaam on building his Parisian culinary empire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1ed9b8a54511cbeb19c762d25edb2ad608cfe390eabfc16043834033595cfc7f</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:57:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T14:56:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261109-chef-alan-geaam-on-building-his-parisian-culinary-empire--fcaad66b2ec1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261109-chef-alan-geaam-on-building-his-parisian-culinary-empire" /><summary type="html">In this edition of Entre Nous, we are delighted to welcome Alan Geaam, a Michelin-starred chef who arrived in Paris in 1999 with a one-way ticket and nothing more than a backpack. Now, 27 years on, he's the founder of a multi-million-euro restaurant empire. He tells us about his journey to success and how he honours his Lebanese roots through his cooking.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>Russell Brand sentenced to 10 years, 6 months for rape and sexual assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:768243167342726a92720b85873d9303e67c41082cc1c8d74a16b0aff42f1869</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:58:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T14:45:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-russell-brand-sentenced-to-10-years-6-months-for-rape-and-sexual-assault--3be1a4c1e376.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-russell-brand-sentenced-to-10-years-6-months-for-rape-and-sexual-assault" /><summary type="html">Comedian Russell ​Brand, once one ‌of Britain's most high-profile broadcasters, ⁠was sentenced to 10-and-a-half years in prison on Monday after he was convicted of raping one woman and ‌sexually assaulting three more around two decades ago.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France brings forward minimum wage increase in bid to quell unrest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5a611cbb893bf43fac15d1bdc33472b2e9344b6037bf53156cdbd8d01f74b8f</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:58:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T14:43:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-france-brings-forward-minimum-wage-increase-in-bid-to-quell-unrest--bcd1f89339ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-france-brings-forward-minimum-wage-increase-in-bid-to-quell-unrest" /><summary type="html">French Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu said ​on Monday he was bringing forward a planned 1.6 percent hike in the minimum wage to December from January, as he sought to defuse a cost-of-living crisis that has sparked some of France's worst civil unrest in years. It comes as Lecornu meets labour groups on Monday in a bid to find solutions to the cost-of-living crisis. France 24's Rochelle Ferguson has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>COP31: Betting on electricity to break the climate deadlock</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a833422a73a281d6b6e2bf5d03082e2683fcc4950f21c674856f837c312421f6</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:58:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T14:33:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/environment/20261109-cop31-betting-on-electricity-to-break-the-climate-deadlock--72ee551da13a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/environment/20261109-cop31-betting-on-electricity-to-break-the-climate-deadlock" /><summary type="html">From November 9 to 20, the international community is gathering in Antalya, Turkey, for the UN COP31 conference. At a time when the energy crisis linked to the war in the Middle East has forced countries to confront their dependence on fossil fuels, this new round of climate negotiations is starting off with a new goal: to push for a massive shift toward electricity.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Saving the Venetian lagoon: A natural buffer against climate change</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:86e5db2e4db7682e30dc6f5c5322b55a8b58b6d32901da95c30b9b6c02446ef2</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:58:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T14:18:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261109-saving-the-venetian-lagoon-a-natural-buffer-against-climate-change--0c07a9ddcfbf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261109-saving-the-venetian-lagoon-a-natural-buffer-against-climate-change" /><summary type="html">The Venetian lagoon is home to "barene" – salt marshes made of vegetation and mud, which play an important role against the effects of climate breakdown. They absorb CO2 and can store it long term in the soil, even more efficiently than land forests. But erosion and rising sea levels are threatening these natural ramparts. Today, scientists and environmental associations are trying to save these unique ecosystems. Our Italy correspondent Natalia Mendoza reports.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>'Crumbs': French PM's 1.6% minimum wage increase fails to placate unions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b78efe2f6753caef08d379e939c2ab1f786bce702473cb3f9b911d40481c390c</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:58:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T13:52:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261109-french-pm-lecornu-announces-increase-minimum-wage-bid-to-calm-protests--c75a86d96f1c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261109-french-pm-lecornu-announces-increase-minimum-wage-bid-to-calm-protests" /><summary type="html">French Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu announced on Monday that a planned 1.6% increase in the minimum wage would be brought forward from January to December after holding talks with trade unions and business leaders over the cost-of-living crisis that has fuelled weeks of unrest across France. The increase fell well short of the demands of unions, which have called for fresh protests in the coming days.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Iran 'has mistaken perception' of US midterm result, expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:74647dac38acec75e8379c6216038cfab6caee315282a52edb3f972f4ba116e5</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:58:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T13:49:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-sees-golden-opportunity-for-a-sweetheart-deal-after-us-midterms-expert-says--83d8e60dc207.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-sees-golden-opportunity-for-a-sweetheart-deal-after-us-midterms-expert-says" /><summary type="html">A leading commentator on Iran says the country sees the results of the US midterm elections as giving them a golden opportunity for a sweet deal. Paymon Azmoudeh from Forward Global was speaking amid conflicting statements from the key players about whether there will be further US military action in Iran. President Donald Trump says that renewed strikes on Iran are "highly unlikely" if talks progress. However, Iran's foreign minister says the midterms have brought a ⁠pause to mediators' work.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>All eyes on Rubio as Iran, Ukraine set to dominate G7 meeting in Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10d45f24a94a0d07aa420ddc0f7db17770d9725cbad2d6b7bfd82a2c5d0d9aac</id><updated>2026-11-09T18:58:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T13:45:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-all-eyes-on-rubio-as-iran-ukraine-set-to-dominate-g7-meeting-in-paris--dd55302d84d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-all-eyes-on-rubio-as-iran-ukraine-set-to-dominate-g7-meeting-in-paris" /><summary type="html">G7 foreign ministers began two days of talks in Paris on Monday as they grapple with multiple unresolved global crises. US Secretary of State Marco Rubio is likely to face questions about whether the Trump administration will shift its positions on the conflicts in Ukraine and Iran in particular following the Democrats sweeping victory in the midterms. France 24’s Clovis Casali has more.</summary></entry></feed>
